# scenario 05.7: A note can list the scenarios whose behaviour stays
# Each folder holds a design note of increment 07 with an automated and a
# manual scenario and the section Unchanged behaviour. check-design accepts
# the note in good/, which lists the automated scenario with a reason. It
# rejects the note in manual/, which lists the manual scenario, the note in
# missing/, which lists 07.3, and the note in no-reason/, whose line gives
# no reason.
exec factory check-design good/docs/increments/07-later
stdout '^check-design: ok \d+ checked$'
! stdout ': error '

exitcode 1 factory check-design manual/docs/increments/07-later
stdout '^check-design: error \S*manual/docs/increments/07-later/design\.md:\d+: unknown-scenario( |$)'
stdout '^check-design: 1 errors$'

exitcode 1 factory check-design missing/docs/increments/07-later
stdout '^check-design: error \S*missing/docs/increments/07-later/design\.md:\d+: unknown-scenario( |$)'
stdout '^check-design: 1 errors$'

exitcode 1 factory check-design no-reason/docs/increments/07-later
stdout '^check-design: error \S*no-reason/docs/increments/07-later/design\.md:\d+: bad-unchanged-line( |$)'
stdout '^check-design: 1 errors$'

-- good/docs/increments/07-later/design.md --
# Increment 07: later

## Goal

- The later tool of increment 07 works.

## Out of scope

- Everything else.

## Existing tools

- None found; searched for later tools.

## Interface

- `later run`

## Rollout

- Off switch: none. Failure signal: the tool rejects a correct input.

## Evidence

- Approved scenarios: 07.1.

## Scenarios

- **scenario 07.1** (automated) **A later thing works.** Given a later thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 07.2** (manual) **A person checks it.** Given a later thing, the tool accepts it.

## Unchanged behaviour

- 07.1: the tool before this increment already accepts a later thing.
-- manual/docs/increments/07-later/design.md --
